{\left(1+\dfrac{s}{10}\right)}\] For \(\omega&lt;0.1\,\text{rad/sec}\), neither zero nor pole is activated. \[\therefore G(j\omega)\approx \frac{K(1)}{(1)}\] At \(\omega=0.001\,\text{rad/sec}\), magnitude from the plot is \(0\,\text{dB}\). \[20\log|G(j0.001)|=0\] \[20\log K=0\] \[K=1\] Hence, \[G(s)=(1)\frac{\left(1+\dfrac{s}{0.1}\right)}
{\left(1+\dfrac{s}{10}\right)}\] \[G(s)=\frac{1+10s}{1+0.1s}\] \[\boxed{\text{(A) }\frac{10s+1}{0.1s+1}}\]

From the given signal flow graph, assume the \(\boldsymbol{\dot{x}_{1}}\), \(\boldsymbol{\dot{x}_{2}}\), \(x_1\) and \(x_2\) as: <img src="img/dd9559288372426e.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,416px)"> From the signal flow graph, \[\dot{x}_{1}=-x_{1}+x_{2}\] \[\dot{x}_{2}=-x_{1}+2u\] \[y=0.5(x_{1}+x_{2}) = 0.5x_1 + 0.5x_2\] Therefore, state equations are, \[\frac{d}{dt}
\left[\begin{array}{c}
x_{1}\\
x_{2}
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
-1 &amp; 1\\
-1 &amp; 0
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
x_{1}\\
x_{2}
\end{array}\right]
+
\left[\begin{array}{c}
0\\
2
\end{array}\right]u\] \[y=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0.5 &amp; 0.5
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
x_{1}\\
x_{2}
\end{array}\right]\] \[\boxed{
\text{(D) }
\dot{x}=
\begin{bmatrix}
-1 &amp; 1\\
-1 &amp; 0
